{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1132148-inspiration-for-what-an-awakening-is-like","id":1132148,"title":"Inspiration for what an awakening is like?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-21T03:40:38-07:00","id":1132148,"title":"Inspiration for what an awakening is like?","content":"I'm interested in reading more about what an awakening can be like. Inspirations, ideas from other characters, and so on. Are there are any old sourcebooks from 1e that deals with it? Or if you have any old discussions on the subject. Or really, any ideas for inspiration. <br /> <br /> Considering the name I found it a bit difficult to search for the topic specifically :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11756-razikale","name":"Razikale","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T03:53:46-07:00","id":1132152,"title":"","content":"Did you read the various example Awakenings in the book on pg. 61? They're a good place to start. A friend of mine broke them down into a skeletal story structure that you can build off of.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Acanthus</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> awaken as an exploration of agency.</span></span><ul><li>The Monotony: The destiny set before you</li> <li>The Breakaway: Going against the expected</li> <li>The Stranger: a first brush with Arcadia</li> <li>The Clue That Leads to the Edge of Arcadia: The seeking</li> <li>The Deal: Winning; being your own master</li> <li>The Transformation</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mastigos</span></span><ul><li>The Flaw or Obsession</li> <li>The Descent</li> <li>The Turning Point</li> <li>The Choice: Fix or Crash-and-burn, for good; choose neither</li> <li>The Revelation &amp; Transformation</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Moros</span></span><ul><li>Impending, unavoidable change</li> <li>The resisting, and the pressure increasing</li> <li>The height of intensity</li> <li>The action/choice</li> <li>The transformation</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Obrimos </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">awaken as the logical consequence of their theories and research.</span></span><ul><li>The Logic / Ordered System</li> <li>The flaws in their thinking</li> <li>The Incongruity / Wordless Truth; the Compulsion</li> <li>The Decisive Action: Do or die, command your experience</li> <li>The Transformation</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thyrsus</span></span><ul><li>Living things and the spirits within them</li> <li>The first bit of descent into being a wild one; the first signs of the animistic world</li> <li>They fall off the edge of humanity and into dominance, apex predator or alpha; blatantly supernatural experiences accepted as primal truths</li> <li>They claim their territory and return to the world, evolved</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T08:10:33-07:00","id":1132217,"title":"","content":"Yeah I read those. I was mostly interested in reading even more <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11756-razikale","name":"Razikale","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T08:21:43-07:00","id":1133790,"title":"","content":"I suspect that we will have to wait until either SoS is out or Dave decides to spoil the Awakening chapter to get more material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T08:57:53-07:00","id":1133815,"title":"","content":"There are lots of awakenings described across the line in the sample characters; though they tend to be kinda short.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1132148-inspiration-for-what-an-awakening-is-like?p=1132152#post1132152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A friend of mine broke them down into a skeletal story structure that you can build off of...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really cool. Frankly, I wish that breakdown was in the corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T21:20:24-07:00","id":1134353,"title":"","content":"I like to imagine that during the initial awakening, the Mage is surging with raw power as they become subject to a flood of heightened awareness. At this point, they have the power of an Archmage, but lack the knowledge that comes with it, so their magic fluctuates out of control. Fortunately, this power surge quickly dissipates as their mind and body stabilize.<br /> <br /> It is the memory of that power that inspires the mage to pursue their craft. They know they have the power inside them if they try hard enough. Now all they need is the knowledge of how to access it properly.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-27-2017, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T22:32:37-07:00","id":1134358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1132148-inspiration-for-what-an-awakening-is-like?p=1134353#post1134353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to imagine that during the initial awakening, the Mage is surging with raw power as they become subject to a flood of heightened awareness. At this point, they have the power of an Archmage, but lack the knowledge that comes with it, so their magic fluctuates out of control. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis makes sense. During the Awakening the Mage signs his name to a Watch Tower, creating a sympathetic link that allows him/her to draw down Supernal energies/truth into the Fallen World, but during the Awakening process his soul has a direct link to a Supernal realm. The Mage is overwhelmed by a flood of Supernal symbols and stands outside the rules of the Fallen World. In that moment he has access to the power to rewrite the world but lacks the knowledge to consciously wield it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 